{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then answered Eliphaz the Temanite, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If one assay to commune with thee, wilt thou be grieved?\nBut who can withhold himself from speaking?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, thou hast instructed many,\nAnd thou hast strengthened the weak hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy words have upholden him that was falling,\nAnd thou hast made firm the feeble knees.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now it is come unto thee, and thou faintest;\nIt toucheth thee, and thou art troubled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is not thy fear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy confidence,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the integrity of thy ways thy hope?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember, I pray thee, who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ever",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perished, being innocent?\nOr where were the upright cut off?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "According as I have seen, they that plow iniquity,\nAnd sow trouble, reap the same.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By the breath of God they perish,\nAnd by the blast of his anger are they consumed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The roaring of the lion, and the voice of the fierce lion,\nAnd the teeth of the young lions, are broken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The old lion perisheth for lack of prey,\nAnd the whelps of the lioness are scattered abroad.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now a thing was secretly brought to me,\nAnd mine ear received a whisper thereof.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In thoughts from the visions of the night,\nWhen deep sleep falleth on men,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fear came upon me, and trembling,\nWhich made all my bones to shake.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then a spirit passed before my face;\nThe hair of my flesh stood up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It stood still, but I could not discern the appearance thereof;\nA form was before mine eyes:",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "There was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " silence, and I heard a voice, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saying",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ",",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall mortal man be more just than God?\nShall a man be more pure than his Maker?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he putteth no trust in his servants;\nAnd his angels he chargeth with folly:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How much more them that dwell in houses of clay,\nWhose foundation is in the dust,\nWho are crushed before the moth!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Betwixt morning and evening they are destroyed:\nThey perish for ever without any regarding it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.4.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.4.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is not their tent-cord plucked up within them?\nThey die, and that without wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
